From af1c2f05234a16374891d3db2e40ee0aee427f9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: khegazy <address removed>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:58:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] A linear drag and a forcing shell for stationary 2D
 turbulence: the linear law takes a negative constant rate, and random_modes
 takes a minimum_mode

The linear law's config accepted only a positive rate. Under the constant policy a negative
rate is a linear drag on the velocity fluctuation, the large-scale friction that arrests the
inverse cascade of forced two-dimensional turbulence; its half-step denominator 1 - dt rate / 2
then exceeds one, so the existing half step and time-step check hold unchanged. The config
now refuses only a zero rate, and a non-positive rate under the adaptive policies.

random_modes forced every mode inside maximum_mode, a ball that includes the box scale. The
optional minimum_mode confines the force to the shell between the two radii. It is None by
default, so it stays out of the exclude_none physics hash and existing identities do not
move; it enters the checkpoint settings, so a carry of the ball law does not resume a shell
law.

Tests: the config accepts a negative constant rate and refuses it under each adaptive
policy, and takes or refuses a shell; the drag removes energy, adds no net momentum and
splits its force at its rate; the shell law selects exactly the ball's modes at or beyond
the inner radius, has no Fourier content inside it, refuses a ball carry and an empty shell.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <address removed>
